title VOLS-J13r2 — the survey sites classified by kind and guard
prompt Continue the autonomous loop: climb the next agent-doable crux (VOLS-J13r2), send each finished increment as its own signed round.
think r1 proved the census is complete by construction. r2's crux: classify each site so the molt (LOWE) knows exactly what to touch and the guard knows exactly what to grow to cover.
think Two classifications: kind (prose relabel-target vs kept witness handle whose filename carries the ordinal — Keaton's prose-only ruling keeps tools/granary_lap1.rish and kin) and guard (already-watched vs gap).
think Derived "guarded" from the guard in force: vols_guardlist_extract.sh pulls the 29 scanned paths from cion_module_labeling_witness's own labeling_module_scan.sh invocation, so guarded is never a hand-copy beside the guard.
think The crux invariant fell out cleanly: because the CION guard passes GREEN, every guarded file carries no bare ordinal, so no site can sit in a guarded file — guarded_sites is 0 by construction. The classifier proves it (and bites a planted drifted guarded file in the negative fixture, verdict=drift) rather than assuming it.
obs Live classification of the 223 sites: 144 are kept witness handles, only 79 are prose gaps — the real LOWE relabel worklist, an order of magnitude smaller than the raw site count, and guarded_sites=0 (guard and sites disjoint). Naming the kinds turned a scary 223 into an honest 79.
obs Gave r2 its own fixture tree (vols_classify_tree/) so r1's witness asserts (surfaces=3, sites=1) stay untouched — additive, no shared-fixture coupling.
loom witness=vols_classify_witness live_sites=223 live_handles=144 live_prose_gaps=79 guarded_sites=0
